I found the precise cause in Whyline 0.3.37.1: a chat turn commits first and appends `chat-history.jsonl` afterward, so that file is guaranteed to look dirty when Relay checks the tree. I’m applying a reversible, repository-local workaround: checkpoint the existing history, hide only that append-only file from Git’s worktree check during the relay, and leave all source files fully visible. I will not use `--allow-dirty`.
